<body bgcolor="#666666">

    

      <table>

    

      <td bordercolor="#000000" bgcolor="#666666"> <!-- InstanceBeginEditable name="centerContent" -->
        <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
<tr>
            <td bgcolor="#333333" class="content"><strong><font color="#CCCCCC">Welcome</font></strong></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="content"><br>
              <font size="4">Welcome to WoL'sLan Page. </font>
              <p>
              <font color="#FFFFFF">If you are having Problems Signing up try this Link ---
</font> <a href="http://wol.awoodman.net/members/Default.asp" target="_blank">
            <font size="3" color="#FFFFFF">http://wol.awoodman.net/members/</font></a><font size="3"><br>

              
              </p>
              <p><b>4/12/02 --- Other LAN's</b><div>
<p><font face="Arial" size="2">VaultLan</font></div>
            <div>
              <font size="3">&nbsp;</font></div>
            <div>
              <font face="Arial" size="2"><a href="http://thevault.zapto.org">
              <font size="3">http://thevault.zapto.org</font></a></font></div>
              <p>
              <font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" color="#00cc00" size="2">
              LanFest...<br>
              <br>
              <font color="#ffffff">Where:<br>
              </font>Cannington Showgrounds<br>
              <br>
              <font color="#ffffff">Dates:</font><br>
              First Day - 10am Sat - 7am Sun<br>
              2nd Day - 8am Sun - 5pm Sun<br>
              <br>
              <font color="#ffffff">Costs:</font><br>
              First Day - $15<br>
              2nd Day - $8<br>
              Both - $20<br>
              <br>
              <font color="#ffffff">URL<font color="#00cc00">:<br>
              </font></font>
              <a href="http://lanfest.rfgt.net" style="text-decoration: none; font-family: Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; font-style: normal; line-height: normal; color: #FFFFFF; background-color: #666666">
              http://lanfest.rfgt.net</a></font><p><span class="RSS:item">
            <font size="3">The last big CGG Lan for the year will be 21st DEC 
            Check it outl.<br><a href="http://members.iinet.net.au/~tcoc/cgg/">
            <font size="4">http://members.iinet.net.au/~tcoc/cgg/</font></a></font></span><p>&nbsp;<p><b>2/12/02 --- SouthLAN</b><p>The guys from SouthLAN will be 
            joining us at the next LAN. Its looking like we will be rocking at 
            this LAN<p><b>2/12/02 --- LAN</b><p>Less then 2 weeks to go until the LAN. 
            Let get ready ppl, if you have not yet signed up get cracking as we 
            are hoping for a big LAN.<p><b>27/11/02 --- What's up</b><p>Hey ppl Jump on to the Forum 
            and let us know what you what at the next LAN.<p><b>21/11/02 --- Hi</b><p>Hi everybody,<p>Just a quick note to 
            say all looks good for the next LAN. We are hoping for a Big turnout 
            for the last LAN of the year. Stay tuned for more updates.<p><b>10/11/02 --- Thank you</b><p>Well another LAN over. We all 
            had a great time playing MoH:AA and the demo of MoH:AAS (Spearhead) 
            which looks like it will be a very big game and the next LAN. I 
            would just like to thank all the ppl that attended and a couple of 
            ppl that helped out. Thanks to Campbell,&nbsp; Nic (from West-LAN), 
            GazMan (from SouthLAN), Rebecca for running the snack bar, and 
            Maxxim, Milo and Nevyn for helping with the clean up. 
              <p><b>8/11/02 --- DATABASE PROBLEMS</b><p>Hey ppl,<p>We have has a 
            small problem with the members database so if you could please check 
            if you are still registered as a member (it should only be if you 
            have registered within the last week).<p>Sorry about that.... See 
            you at the LAN<p>WoL<p><b>7/11/02 --- WoL'sLAN 5</b><p>Not long to go !!!! 
              <p>We provide :<br>
              - one power point (so if you need to bring a double adaptor)<br>
              - one port on the switch<br>
              - There will be some extra network cable but not enough for 
              everyone<br>
              <br>
              If you use INTERNET CONNECTION SHARING *** PLEASE TURN IT OFF ***<br>
              <br>
              Please do not use the use the NET SEND command, if you will like 
              to chat with ppl or message ppl use the DC chat window.<br>
              <br>
              We will be running a MoH Tournament (like the last one)<br>
              - 5 per team<br>
              - Round based<br>
              - Maps will be desided on the day<br>
              - Now as for prizes, we have not followed up and sponsership for 
              this LAN (sorry that was my job :( ) So we will be giving away 
              Chocolates to the winning team. If this is a problem then please 
              let me know :)<br>
&nbsp;<p><b>5/11/02 --- Tournament</b><p>It look like we will be running 
            a MoH Comp. Not sure on the details, it will just be for a bit of 
            fun
    <img alt="Rocks!" src="http://filefreaks.fragland.net/images/smilies/rock.gif" align="middle" border="0"><p><span class="smalltext"><b>1/11/02 --- How to Disable Net Send
              in Windows XP</b></span>
              <p><span class="largetext">Alright guys, what you've all been
              waiting for.<br>
              <br>
              To Disable Net Send:<br>
              <br>
              * Right Click on 'My Computer' select 'Manage'<br>
              * Select 'Services and Applications'<br>
              * Select 'Services'<br>
              * Right Click on the service called 'Messenger' and click 'Stop'<br>
              <br>
              Done. You will no longer recieve Net Sends. Note for future
              reference that this does not affect Windows Messenger - it will
              still work.<br>
              <br>
              To turn it back on, do the same, but click 'Start'.<br>
              <br>
              OK Wol, next job?<br>
              <br>
              Have a good Wolslan ! <img alt="biggrin.gif" src="biggrin.gif" border="0"></span></p>
              <p>--- OakMan</p>
              <p><b>29/10/02 --- Message</b></p>
            <p><font color="#00FFFF">OakMan:</font>
            <font color="#00FF00">but they're not Wolslan</font><br>
            <font color="#00FFFF">OakMan: </font><font color="#00FF00">
            wolslan, wolslan, come on in for a wol deal... come on in for a wol 
            deal</font></p>
            <p><b>28/10/02 --- SIGNUP's</b></p>
            <p>Ok if you are having trouble signing up it may have some thing to 
            do with your cookies. You can try changing your cookies to low.</p>
            <font SIZE="2">
            <p>under IE go to Tools &gt; Internet Options &gt; Privacy and change the 
            cookies to low this works</p>
            <p>If you are still having problems and you want to signup just 
            email me and I will add you to the list.
          <A href="mailto:redacted@example.com?subject=LAN Site">WoL</A></p>
            </font><p><b>27/10/02 --- OTHER LAN THAT ARE 
            COMING UP</b></p>
            <table borderColor="#000000" cellSpacing="0" cellPadding="0" width="100%" border="1">
              <tr bgColor="#ffffff">
                <td borderColor="#ffffff"><font size="2">Hello everyone. I have 
                been informed by the owners of the building that they have found 
                a new tenant to lease it. This means that <b>SOUTHLAN</b> will 
                be closing it's doors. The next Lan is on the <b>2nd of November</b> 
                and the last Lan will be the <b>16th of November</b>. We will 
                over the next 6 weeks be trying to find alternative 
                accommodation to host Southlan at. If anyone has any ideas, or 
                know of a place to host the Lan can they please contact one of 
                us, and we will follow it up. Thanks for all of your support 
                throughout the year.</font></td>
              </tr>
              <tr bgColor="#ffffff">
                <td borderColor="#ffffff" align="right"><font size="2">GazMan</font></td>
              </tr>
            </table>
            <table borderColor="#000000" cellSpacing="0" cellPadding="0" width="100%" border="1">
              <tr bgColor="#ffffff">
                <td borderColor="#ffffff">
                <div>
                  <font face="Arial" size="2">Hey <b>lanfest</b> is </font>&nbsp;</div>
                <div>
                  <font face="Arial" size="2">Time: 11am - 11am</font></div>
                <div>
                  <font face="Arial" size="2">Date: Sat <b>2nd - Sun 3rd 
                  November</b></font></div>
                <div>
                  <font face="Arial" size="2">ppl - 40 - 50</font></div>
                <div>
                  <font face="Arial" size="2">area - Mandurah</font></div>
                <div>
                  &nbsp;<font face="Arial" size="2"><a href="http://www.lanfest.tk">www.lanfest.tk</a> 
                  has all other details and a signup page.</font></div>
                <div>
                  <font face="Arial" size="2">thanx Gareth</font></div>
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr bgColor="#ffffff">
                <td borderColor="#ffffff" align="right">&nbsp;</td>
              </tr>
            </table>
            <table borderColor="#000000" cellSpacing="0" cellPadding="0" width="100%" border="1">
              <tr bgColor="#ffffff">
                <td borderColor="#ffffff">
                <div>
                  <font face="Arial" size="2"><b>3JC</b> are holding a LAN in 
                  mid November and we would like to see as many people there as 
                  possible. This is our first one and we would like to have it a 
                  big success. We are 4 very experienced IT&nbsp;specialists so rest 
                  assured the day will be run in a very professional manner.
                  </font>
                </div>
                <div>
                  &nbsp;</div>
                <div>
                  <font face="Arial" size="2">Time 9 am till ???</font></div>
                <div>
                  <font face="Arial" size="2">Date: <b>Saturday 16 November 2002</b></font></div>
                <div>
                  <font face="Arial" size="2">Numbers limited to 25</font></div>
                <div>
                  <font face="Arial" size="2">Area: Safety Bay</font></div>
                <div>
                  <font face="Arial" size="2">Contact
                  <a href="mailto:redacted@example.com">redacted@example.com</a>&nbsp;for 
                  an information pack and to register you interest.</font></div>
                <div>
                  <font face="Arial" size="2">Big Thanks to WoL for posting this 
                  for us.</font></div>
                <div>
                  <font face="Arial" size="2">Hope to see you there.</font></div>
                <div>
                  &nbsp;</div>
                <div>
                  <font face="Arial" size="2">John :)</font></div>
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr bgColor="#ffffff">
                <td borderColor="#ffffff" align="right">&nbsp;</td>
