            </table>
            <p>&nbsp;</p>
            <p><b>23/10/02 --- WoL'sLAN 5</b></p>
            <p><span class="largetext"><span style="COLOR: blue">
            <img alt="lol.gif" src="lol.gif" border="0">
            <img alt="lol.gif" src="lol.gif" border="0">
            <img alt="lol.gif" src="lol.gif" border="0">
            <img alt="lol.gif" src="lol.gif" border="0">
            <img alt="lol.gif" src="lol.gif" border="0">
            <img alt="lol.gif" src="lol.gif" border="0">
            <img alt="lol.gif" src="lol.gif" border="0">
            <img alt="lol.gif" src="lol.gif" border="0">
            <img alt="lol.gif" src="lol.gif" border="0">
            </span><br>Hey Hey ppl <br>
            The Next LAN is Fast approaching <br>
            <br>
            <img alt="doubleenforce.gif" src="doubleenforce.gif" border="0"> 
            Saturday 9th November
            <img alt="doubleenforce.gif" src="doubleenforce.gif" border="0">
            <br>
            <br>
            Still trying to sort out the new sign-up stuff <br>
            but if you haven't signed up in the members <br>
            section check it out. <br>
            <br>
            Ok I'm sure the LAN will fill fast so be quick <br>
            and start getting ready for another great LAN <br>
            lets see if we can get 80 ppl attend this LAN
            <span style="COLOR: blue"><br>
            <img alt="lol.gif" src="lol.gif" border="0">
            <img alt="lol.gif" src="lol.gif" border="0">
            <img alt="lol.gif" src="lol.gif" border="0">
            <img alt="lol.gif" src="lol.gif" border="0">
            <img alt="lol.gif" src="lol.gif" border="0">
            <img alt="lol.gif" src="lol.gif" border="0">
            <img alt="lol.gif" src="lol.gif" border="0">
            <img alt="lol.gif" src="lol.gif" border="0">
            <img alt="lol.gif" src="lol.gif" border="0">
            </span></span><span class="smalltext"><br>
&nbsp;</span></p>
            <p><b>18/10/02 --- New Question</b></p>
            <p>New Mini Poll Question :)</p>
            <p><b>16/10/02 --- Members Section</b></p>
            <p>Hey ppl, we are changing the sign-ups. As you may have seen there 
            is now a members section on the left. In this section you can add 
            and remove your name from the LANs. It is still constructed, but 
            should all work, if you have any problems let me know. </p>
            <p><b>14/10/02 --- Thank you</b></p>
            <p>Well another great LAN over and done with. I would just like to 
            thank a couple of ppl for helping out. Campbell and Ashley for 
            helping me setup and run the event. Adam for running the snack bar 
            for most of the night, the Guys from SouthLAN for the loan of some 
            tables and some switches, and to all the ppl that turned up and made 
            the night heaps of fun.</p>
            <p>As soon as we book the hall for the next LAN I will let you all 
            know. Thanks again to all the ppl that turned up&nbsp; :)</p>
            <p><b>10/10/02 --- LAN Stuff</b></p>
            <p>The LAN starts 12 noon and finishes around 3am.</p>
            <p>Once again we will be ordering pizza's about 6pm from Eagle Boys 
            Pizza.</p>
            <p>We will be selling : <br></p>
            <blockquote>
            <p>Coke / Fanta 600ml&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; - $1.50 
            (Sorry about the price increase we could not help it)<br>
            M&M's / Skittles 55grms&nbsp; - $1.00<br>
            King Size Crunchies - $1.50<br>
            Masters Ice Coffee<br>
            and Choc Milk 600ml&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; - $1.50<br>
            Pizza&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 
            - $5.00</p> 
            </blockquote>
            <p><b>7/10/02 --- LAN is this weekend</b></p>
            <p>Get ready ppl, LAN is this weekend.</p>
            <p><b>4/10/02 --- WoL'sLAN 4</b></p>
            <p>Ok after I emailed all the ppl have have signed up for the LAN, 
            some ppl have got back to be telling me that they cant make it. So I 
            have about 5 extra seat available for the LAN. So if you are 
            interested then please email me and I will get back to you ASAP.</p>
            <p><b>28/9/02 --- LAN FULL</b></p>
            <p>Ok the LAN is full. If you cant make it can you please contact me 
            so I can remove your name.</p>
            <p><b>23/9/02 --- WALAN</b></p>
            <p>Some ppl have shown some interest in going to WALAN. Some of us 
            have booked a seat for Day 2 and we are got to be on Table 1.</p>
            <p>In other news we still have 3 weeks to go until the next LAN and 
            we already have over 70 ppl booked, Looks like we are up for another 
            big LAN :)</p>
            <p><b>9/9/02 --- Signup's For WoL'sLAN 4</b></p>
            <p>The Signups are open for the next LAN</p>
            <p><b>8/9/02 --- WoL'sLAN 4</b></p>
            <p>Well we will be looking at having the next LAN on the 12th of 
            October. We will be trying for 80 ppl again. More info to come.</p>
            <p><b>2/9/02 --- WoL'sLan 3</b></p>
            <p>Thanks to every one for attending, everything went well after 
            some initial power problems. We had a total of approx 70ppl attend. </p>
            <p>The MoH:AA comp has been run and won.</p>
            <p>Head on over to the
            <a href="http://forums.west-lan.net/viewforum.php?f=8">Forums</a> 
            and tell us what you thought of WoL'sLan 3 </p>
            <p><b>29/8/2002 --- SIGNUP's</b></p>
            <p><br>
              We have almost reached 80 ppl, I still don't know how but we have done 
            it. And we are sorry but as soon as we reach 80 we can not except any more signups :( <br><br>
            So if you can make it please let be know so we can remove your name off the list. Anyway hope to see you all on Saturday at the LAN<br>
            hfph</p>
            <p><b>28/8/2002 --- Snack Bar</b></p>
            <p>We will have a Snack Bar again.<br><br>
            We will be selling : <br></p>
            <blockquote>
            <p>Coke / Fanta 600ml&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; - $1.00<br>
            Muffins&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 
            - $0.50 <br>
            Masters Ice Coffee<br>
            and Choc Milk 600ml&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; - $1.50<br>
            Pizza&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 
            - $5.00<br>
            (The Pizza will be ordered for 6pm)</p> 
            </blockquote>
            <p>&nbsp;</p>
            <p><b>26/8/2002 --- SIGNUP's </b></p>
            <p>Due the abundance of ppl signing up for the LAN we have to set 
            the limit on 
            the signup's, we have over booking and are now looking into hiring 
            some extra equipment for the LAN. With this equipment we should be 
            able to cater for <font size="2"><b>80</b></font><b><font size="2"> ppl</font></b>.<br><br>If you have signed up but you cant 
            make it please let us know. We are hoping for 80 ppl with the extra 
            equipment.</p>
            <p><b>22/8/2002 --- Next LAN</b></p>
            <p>Just an update we have hit 50 ppl signed up. We are looking at 
            another big LAN :) </p>
            <p><b>19/8/2002 --- UPDATE</b></p>
            <p>Well The Next LAN is on its was with less then 2 weeks to go. We 
            already have heaps of ppl signed up so is you are planing on coming 
            you better get your name on the list.<br>
            <br>
            Have you got a Team ready for the Tournament ? 
            If so Email <A href="mailto:redacted@example.com?subject=LAN Tournament">KiwiSx</A> 
            and register your team so we can start setting up the Tournament. 
            You can also register your team on the day. </p>
            <p><b>11/8/2002 --- Tournament</b></p>
            <p>We are looking at running a tournament in everyone's favourite 
            game Medal of Honour : Allied Assault. The tournament will be teams 
            based with 5 people per team and enough rounds to decide a winning 
            team. A couple of our sponsors 
            <a href="http://www.alienware.com/index.asp?from=WoLNielsen:01_button_120x30" target="_blank">Alienware</a>
             and <a href="http://www.geargrip.com" target="_blank">Geargrip</a> have provided 
            us with some cools stuff as prizes for the winning team. So organise 
            a team. </p>
            <p><b>4/8/2002 --- Forums</b></p>
            <p>New URL <a href="http://WWW.WOLSLAN.NET">WWW.WOLSLAN.NET</a> !!!!</p>
            <p>The West-LAN site is still down so I have changed the Forum Link 
            back to the old Forum.</p>
            <p>Pictures from the last LAN have been added so check them out &lt;&lt; <a href="Pictures.asp">Pictures</a> 
            &gt;&gt;</p>
            <p><b>1/8/2002 --- Forums</b></p>
            <p>Sorry ppl but yes the Forums are DOWN atm (at the moment). The 
            guys at West-LAN let us use there forums (so no adds), but there 
            server has gone down, so please stay with us. If the site is not 
            back up by Friday then I'll change back to the old forum.</p>
            <p><b>30/7/2002 --- Booked</b></p>
            <p>Hall Booked for Saturday the 31 August...</p>
            <p><span style="background-color: #666666; font-weight:700">
            29/7/2002 --- Thanks</span></p>
            <p>Thankyou very much to all the people at attended the LAN on the 
            Saturday 27 July. We had about 45 people with computers turn up and all 
            went well.<br><br>
            The games played included:<br>
            MoH:AA,<br>
            RTCW (once we got it going),<br>
            Mobile Forces (but not enough of it),<br>
            SoF2,<br>
            some Warcraft 3<br>
            and Im sure that CS was going on some were behind my back (hehehehe)<br><br>
            Now the question that is being asked is when is the next 
            LAN. We are hope to have the LAN's 6 weeks apart I know some ppl at 
            the LAN were asking for the LAN to become closer together we will 
            look into this.<br>
            We would like to here your feed back, about the Last 
            LAN and also any ideas you would have about the next LAN. Feel free 
            to email me (<A href="mailto:redacted@example.com">WoL</A>) or hop on to our <a href="http://pub7.ezboard.com/bwolslaning">Forum</a> and leave us a message.<br>
            <br>
            I would just like to thank a couple of ppl:<br>
            Timmy and Adam for Selling the Drinks and organising the Pizza.<br>
            Campbell for organising the Power layout (that all went really well)<br>
            Nic for running the DHCP, DNS and the intranet<br>
            And Paul from Synchro Computers for Loaning us 2 servers<br>
            We Hope to see you all at the next LAN !!!!
            <p><b>21/7/2002 --- LAN soon !!!</b></p>
            <p>Just a quick update. One week to go, the LAN starts at 12 noon 
            and finishes about 3am. We will be running Direct Connect for some 
            file swap, instead of Windows file share. The games we will be 
            playing will include MoH:AA, RTCW, Mobile Forces, Warcraft 3 and 
            UT2003 Demo.<br>
            <br>
            We will be running a DHCP server, so please set automatically obtain an IP, and please turn off Internet sharing. </p>
            <p><b>12/7/2002 --- Snack Bar</b></p>
            <p>We will have a Snack Bar at next LAN, run buy Tim.<br><br>
            We will be selling : <br></p>
            <blockquote>
            <p>Coke / Fanta 600ml&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; - $1.00<br>
            M&M's / Skittles 55grms&nbsp; - $1.00<br>
            Masters Ice Coffee<br>
            and Choc Milk 600ml&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; - $1.50<br>
            Pizza&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 
            - $5.00</p> 
            </blockquote>
            <p><b>3/7/2002</b><p>Well the next LAN is approaching fast, so I 
            hope all of you are ready for some great gaming. We have still not 
            finalised what games we are going to try and run on the night, but 
            I'll try and get a list up soon (not that it really matters what 
            games we say, Im sure ppl will play what ever they want). <p><b>26/6/2002</b><p>Some people have requested some heating for 
            the next LAN, however this is not feasible, unless we increase the 
            entry fee and this is something that we are not really willing to 
            do.<p>So people please remember that it can get a little cold during 
            the night so bring along some warm clothes. <p>
            <span style="background-color: #666666; font-weight:700">20/6/2002</span><p>Ok We have book the Hall for the 27th of 
            July, Its all go !!!<br>
              &nbsp;<p><span style="background-color: #666666; font-weight:700">18/6/2002</span></p>
            <p>Thankyou to all the people at attended my LAN on the 
            Saturday 15 June. We had 40 people with computers turn up and all 
            went well. Now the question that is being asked is when is the next 
            LAN. Well we are looking at having the next LAN is about 6 weeks, we 
            have to make sure that the Hall is not booked.</p>
            <p>I hope you all had fun and look forward to seeing you at the next 
            LAN.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="content">&nbsp;</td>
          </tr>
        </table>
</body>